{
  "apiVersion": 1,
  "type": "docs.node",
  "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
  "data": {
    "id": "astryx:artifact:v1/%40astryxdesign%2Fcli/namespace/global",
    "route": "global",
    "kind": "namespace",
    "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
    "title": "Global mode",
    "summary": "Install Astryx once on your computer and use it in any folder. Each project still runs its own version of Astryx, so a global install never changes what a project gets.",
    "breadcrumb": [],
    "slots": [
      {
        "name": "guides",
        "title": "Global mode, question by question",
        "children": [
          {
            "route": "global/project-global-or-both",
            "name": "project-global-or-both",
            "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
            "kind": "generic",
            "title": "Project, global, or both",
            "summary": "Install Astryx in each project and once for your computer: both is the recommended setup, and the two never conflict. What each side gives you, and how to set it up."
          },
          {
            "route": "global/install-once",
            "name": "install-once",
            "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
            "kind": "generic",
            "title": "Install Astryx globally",
            "summary": "Install the Astryx CLI once for your computer with npm, pnpm, Yarn, Bun, or Volta, and what happens when you are offline."
          },
          {
            "route": "global/who-answers",
            "name": "who-answers",
            "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
            "kind": "generic",
            "title": "Which version runs, and why",
            "summary": "Inside a project, the project's own CLI answers, whichever astryx command you start; in a project with only Core, the astryx command you started answers. Outside a project, your global install answers. How to see which one did."
          },
          {
            "route": "global/updates",
            "name": "updates",
            "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
            "kind": "generic",
            "title": "Updates and notices",
            "summary": "Your global install checks for a newer version once a day and prints a two-line notice after a command succeeds. It never upgrades itself or a project."
          },
          {
            "route": "global/computer-agent-guide",
            "name": "computer-agent-guide",
            "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
            "kind": "generic",
            "title": "The agent guide on your computer",
            "summary": "Your global install keeps one short Astryx skill in your home folder and links it into the folders agent tools read, so agents anywhere know Astryx is there. `astryx init --user` writes it now or turns it off."
          },
          {
            "route": "global/computer-integrations",
            "name": "computer-integrations",
            "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
            "kind": "generic",
            "title": "Integrations installed globally",
            "summary": "Integrations installed next to your global install work in folders outside any project. Inside a project, only the integrations the project installs work, and the others are listed as ones you could add."
          },
          {
            "route": "global/monorepos",
            "name": "monorepos",
            "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
            "kind": "generic",
            "title": "Monorepos and nested folders",
            "summary": "How Astryx finds the project a folder belongs to, and which version answers in a monorepo, a nested app, or a cloned repository inside another project."
          },
          {
            "route": "global/ci-and-containers",
            "name": "ci-and-containers",
            "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
            "kind": "generic",
            "title": "CI and containers",
            "summary": "What Astryx does in CI and containers: no update checks or notices, the project's version as always, and how to cache versions or work with a read-only home folder."
          },
          {
            "route": "global/problems",
            "name": "problems",
            "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
            "kind": "generic",
            "title": "Troubleshooting global mode",
            "summary": "Every line Astryx prints in global mode, what it means, and what to do. Plus the install problems package managers cause: permissions, PATH, Corepack, and Windows."
          },
          {
            "route": "global/uninstall",
            "name": "uninstall",
            "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
            "kind": "generic",
            "title": "Uninstall and reset",
            "summary": "Remove your global install, the agent guide it keeps, and the folders it uses, or reset them to start over."
          },
          {
            "route": "global/reference",
            "name": "reference",
            "package": "@astryxdesign/cli",
            "kind": "generic",
            "title": "Global mode reference",
            "summary": "Every folder global mode uses on each system, the environment variables it reads, the JSON fields it adds, its error codes, and a short glossary."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "Global mode means installing the Astryx CLI once for your computer, so the astryx command works everywhere: in your projects, in an empty folder, and for every coding agent. Inside a project, the project's own version of Astryx answers, so your global install never changes what a project gets."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "lang": "bash",
        "code": "npm install -g @astryxdesign/cli"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "text": "What you get"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "style": "unordered",
        "items": [
          "Docs, components, templates, and search in any folder, before you have a project.",
          "Every coding agent on your computer knows Astryx, through a short guide the CLI keeps where agent tools look.",
          "Each project keeps its own version: in a project, the project's version answers, whichever astryx command you run."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Which version runs"
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "headers": [
          "Where you run it",
          "Which version answers"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Inside a project",
            "The project's own CLI. In a project that installs only `@astryxdesign/core`, the astryx command you started, with a hint once a day to add the CLI."
          ],
          [
            "Outside any project",
            "Your global version."
          ],
          [
            "Commands for your computer, such as `astryx init --user`",
            "Your global version, in any folder."
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "Not sure whether you want a project install, a global one, or both: `astryx docs global/project-global-or-both`. The details: `astryx docs global/who-answers`."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Updates"
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "Your global install never upgrades itself or a project. When a newer version is out, a command that succeeds ends with a two-line notice, at most once a day: `astryx docs global/updates`."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Agents"
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "The CLI keeps a short Astryx guide where agent tools look in your home folder, so an agent working anywhere knows Astryx is there: `astryx docs global/computer-agent-guide`."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Integrations"
      },
      {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "Integrations you install next to your global install work outside projects. Inside a project, only the project's own integrations do: `astryx docs global/computer-integrations`. Building one: `astryx docs authoring/global-integrations`."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "text": "More"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "style": "unordered",
        "items": [
          "Install, and work offline: `astryx docs global/install-once`.",
          "Monorepos and nested folders: `astryx docs global/monorepos`.",
          "CI and containers: `astryx docs global/ci-and-containers`.",
          "Something looks wrong: `astryx docs global/problems`.",
          "Uninstall and reset: `astryx docs global/uninstall`.",
          "Every path, setting, JSON field, and error code: `astryx docs global/reference`.",
          "What each command does outside a project: `astryx docs cli/commands`."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "links": {
      "up": "astryx docs"
    }
  },
  "meta": {
    "answeredBy": {
      "cli": "0.7.12",
      "core": "0.7.12",
      "copy": "carried"
    }
  }
}
